    board(qa): file CF-192 — the public-bind auth gate is OFF whenever a listener already holds the port
    
    Re-verification of the same-tick delivery found the prior execution's drafted but unfiled
    finding still live at the published tip e0e73bd, so this execution files it via the clone
    transport (the canonical checkout is being written by a sibling lane; it is left untouched).
    
    Measured at e0e73bd from a fresh clone of the published remote:
      install-hermes --apply with a listener stub answering on :10800 and a config carrying no
      `dashboard.basic_auth` prints
        PASS  port — listening on :10800
        PASS  status_probe — /api/status -> 200
        HERMES: PASS
        auth_refusal_rows=0
      while the same fixture with `ss` exiting 1 (free port) prints the CF-071 refusal row and
      `HERMES: FAIL (2)` with `auth_refusal_rows=1`.
    
    `scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh:251` guards `check_public_bind_auth` and the gateway start
    with `if ! (… ss -tln | grep -q ":$PORT " )`, so the auth gate is skipped exactly where a
    leftover listener exists, and the adapter certifies that foreign listener as its own. All
    nineteen CF-071 config arms stub `ss` as `exit 1` (`tests/selftest.sh:386`), so no arm exercises
    this branch.
    
    Board append is insert-only: 165 → 166 rows, prefix bytes identical, 0 duplicate ids, one
    `task_created` event (334). No source file changed. `boardctl validate` → RESULT: OK (same 3
    pre-existing warnings as the pre-append board).
    
    The clone ships no `.git/hooks/pre-commit`, so the Tier 1 guard did not run on this commit; the
    gitreins task complete for CF-192 is the gate evidence for this tree.
    
