 {"id": "CF-189", "title": "P3 — OPERATIONS.md marks destroy BLOCKED and forbids guessing bunker flags, while node-create.sh prints an exact `bunker destroy` line that was measured working", "status": "pending", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 2, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-04 by the code-factory-duckbrain-dogfood tick code-factory-duckbrain-dogfood-2026-11-04-08-40-09 (third execution) at origin/main d65adf9, on a real bunker host (server bunker-mvp) and a real public repo (https://github.com/github/gitignore), with the real crier on :8767 reachable from the node (layer-00 `PASS reach:.../health — 200`). `scripts/node-create.sh --project myrepo --repo https://github.com/github/gitignore --harness hermes --ttl 1h` reached NODE INCOMPLETE and its failure path printed: `cleanup required: bunker destroy node-myrepo-042342 --server bunker-mvp` (scripts/node-create.sh:55, incomplete()). That exact line was then run as printed: `bunker destroy node-myrepo-042342 --server bunker-mvp` -> 'Destroying agent node-myrepo-042342 (home 435.2 MB; archiving before delete, deadline 12m0s)…' / 'Agent node-myrepo-042342 destroyed.' / 'Removed local SSH key /home/kara/.config/bunker/keys/node-myrepo-042342', rc=0, and `bunker list --server bunker-mvp` returned to the pre-run two agents. The runbook says the opposite twice: docs/OPERATIONS.md:167 'There is no checked-in command or measured procedure for renewing a bunker agent TTL, destroying an agent … These steps are BLOCKED / NOT YET. Do not guess bunker CLI flags' and :173 'No teardown script is currently tracked … teardown is a manual, operator-owned, BLOCKED change—not a guessed command.' So the one path a new user is told to walk hands them a command their runbook says is unmeasured and forbidden, and the operator cannot tell whether following it is supported. Distinct from the pending CF-150 (nothing stages the gateway auth block, so create can never pass) and CF-179 (the success line prints a literal /home/<uid>): this row is that the documented lifecycle state of destroy is contradicted by the shipped script.", "acceptance_criteria": "0. Reproduce: with CRIER_URL and BUNKER_SERVER set and no node inference key, run the documented create; the failure path prints `cleanup required: bunker destroy <agent> --server <server>`, and running that line destroys the agent (rc=0, archive-then-delete, SSH key removed) as measured above.\n1. Document and script agree: either docs/OPERATIONS.md §8 records destroy as a MEASURED step (naming the run, the date, the archive-before-delete behaviour and the ~435 MB home it archived), or scripts/node-create.sh stops printing a command the runbook forbids. Renew, rebuild and full teardown may stay BLOCKED, but they are separated from destroy instead of sharing its verdict.\n2. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` and `scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK` at the fix commit.", "probe": "grep -n 'cleanup required' scripts/node-create.sh; grep -n 'BLOCKED / NOT YET\\|not a guessed command' docs/OPERATIONS.md | head -4; echo 'measured 2026-11-04: bunker destroy node-myrepo-042342 --server bunker-mvp -> rc=0, \"Agent node-myrepo-042342 destroyed.\", home 435.2 MB archived'", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:28:59Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:28:59Z"}
 {"id":"CF-190","title":"P4 — the configured SSH remote does not authenticate on the fleet control host, so a lane following \"push after commit\" strands its commits and reads a stale origin/main","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":3,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-04 by the code-factory-duckbrain-pm lane on the fleet control host. The registered checkout's `origin` is `git@github.com:coding-hermes/code-factory.git`, so the fleet-wide instruction \"after ANY commit run `git push origin <branch>`\" resolves to an SSH push — which this host cannot perform from an unattended session: `git push origin main` answers `git@github.com: Permission denied (publickey)` (the session's ssh-agent holds no identities and `~/.ssh/code-github.key` is refused), and `git fetch` fails the same way, so a lane's own `origin/main` tracking ref silently stays stale (this pass read a 17-commit-stale ref until it used `git ls-remote`). Consequence measured today: the CF-071 worker's commits `3e6ac40`, `779ab4f`, `1d632d9` and its board closeout `48e1501` sat unpublished from 09:34Z until 09:44Z, and the checkout read `origin/main...HEAD = 0 2` against a ref that named a tip nine commits behind the real remote. The only transport that works here is the HTTPS rewrite through the host's authenticated `gh` credential helper: `git -c url.https://github.com/.insteadOf=git@github.com: push origin main` pushed `caf4364` and `293f7ec` and parity went to `0 0`. GitHub also answered `Internal Server Error` on two consecutive pushes before accepting a third, so a single push attempt is not evidence of a transport failure either. No tracked doc names a supported push path: `grep -n -i 'push|ssh|credential|https' docs/OPERATIONS.md` returns only node-side clone/credential text, `AGENTS.md` carries no push instruction, and `grep -rn 'push' tests/selftest.sh` has no arm that would fail when push auth is broken. Distinct from CF-003 (per-repo deploy keys for cloning on nodes) and from CF-060 (lane_target code identity): this is the control host's publish path for the repo itself. Escape hatch used this tick: HTTPS rewrite with the gh helper, disclosed in the landing messages.","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce on the current tree (from the repo root): `git push --dry-run origin HEAD:main` exits non-zero and prints `git@github.com: Permission denied (publickey)`, while `git -c url.https://github.com/.insteadOf=git@github.com: push --dry-run origin HEAD:main` reaches the remote and prints an up-to-date or would-push line.\n1. One tracked doc (AGENTS.md or docs/OPERATIONS.md) names exactly one supported unattended publish command, states that it uses the host's authenticated credential helper, carries no credential in argv, and quotes the measured exit code it produces on a green run.\n2. A shipped check FAILS with a named row when push authentication is unavailable, so a lane cannot report a landed commit while its push silently died: `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints a `FAIL  push-transport — …` row (never a bare PASS) for a fixture whose push is refused, and a `PASS  push-transport — …` row for a fixture whose push succeeds in the same run.\n3. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` at the fixed tip.","probe":"set +e; ssh_out=$(git push --dry-run origin HEAD:main 2>&1); ssh_rc=$?; https_out=$(git -c \"url.https://github.com/.insteadOf=git@github.com:\" push --dry-run origin HEAD:main 2>&1); https_rc=$?; ssh_line=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$ssh_out\" | grep -m1 'Permission denied' || printf '%s\\n' \"$ssh_out\" | tail -1); https_line=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$https_out\" | tail -1); printf 'ssh_rc=%s %s\\nhttps_rc=%s %s\\n' \"$ssh_rc\" \"$ssh_line\" \"$https_rc\" \"$https_line\"","created_at":"2026-11-04T09:47:26Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T09:53:03Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"e20cddf4572d687d42df268fabd41b204dba7949d2dc5efe25c6dcf95ca380f7"},"foreman_note":"Evidence added 2026-11-04 by the code-factory-pm tick (code-factory-pm-2026-11-04-09-00-57) at 730fee9, measured on this host: SSH publickey is INTERMITTENT, not simply dead. Sequential probes: 'ssh -o BatchMode=yes -T git@github.com' printed 'Hi totalwindupflightsystems!' once (~09:50Z), then 'Permission denied (publickey)' on four consecutive runs, then returned empty (success) again. Every candidate key in ~/.ssh was refused while failing: id_ed25519, id_rsa, id_ed25519_npu, id_ed25519_nas, id_ed25519_m10, id_ed25519_bunker, hermes-hetzner; 'ssh-add -l' reports 'The agent has no identities' (SSH_AUTH_SOCK=/run/user/1000/openssh_agent), so the successes cannot be attributed to a loaded agent identity. A deterministic publish path exists and was used to land cfc017f/40d061e/730fee9: 'gh auth status' shows a valid token with repo scope, and GIT_ASKPASS=<helper that runs 'gh auth token'> GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 git push https://github.com/coding-hermes/code-factory.git main prints 'Everything up-to-date' and 'git ls-remote <https url> refs/heads/main' returns the local HEAD hash. Decidable remedy for this row: make the publish step fall back to that HTTPS+askpass path (token never on a command line) and record which path each push used, rather than retrying SSH blind."}
 {"id":"CF-191","title":"P3 — a Tier-1 PASS is recorded beside a non-zero test-command exit and a `/bin/sh: 1: Bad substitution` line, so the gate's reported exit code disagrees with a direct run","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-04 by the code-factory-pm tick (code-factory-pm-2026-11-04-09-00-57) at tip `1d632d9`.\n\nTHE ANOMALY. The Tier-1 verdict for CF-071 (`.gitreins/history/2026-11-04/eb659af6/verdict.json`, evaluated 2026-11-04T09:40:52Z, commit `1d632d9`) records `tier1` = PASS on all three scanners while its own tier2 note states: \"the script's shell exit code is 2 due to a trailing `/bin/sh: 1: Bad substitution` line printed after `SELFTEST: PASS`\". A gate that reports PASS for a test command whose measured exit code is 2 is not measuring what it claims (AGENTS.md rule 2, \"every check must be able to fail\"); either the exit code belongs to a process other than the suite, or the pass rule ignores it.\n\nTHE DIRECT MEASUREMENT, same tip, three runs. `bash tests/selftest.sh` printed `SELFTEST: PASS` and exited 0 every time, with zero `Bad substitution` lines:\n- one sequential run, `/home/kara/.hermes/cache/scratch/cf-pm-selftest-0920.log` (`SELFTEST_RC=0`),\n- two concurrent runs launched from one checkout by `/home/kara/.hermes/cache/scratch/cf-concurrent-gate.sh` at `1d632d9` — both `SELFTEST: PASS`, `RC_A=0`, `RC_B=0`, `bad-substitution lines: 0`, identical 50 intentional-fixture `FAIL` rows each. Concurrency is therefore refuted as the cause; the suite is repeatable here.\n\nTHE LINE IS NOT RARE. `grep -rl 'Bad substitution' .gitreins/history/` matches 9 files at this tip (for example `2026-11-04/114d78f0/verdict.json`, `2026-11-04/eb659af6/verdict.json`, `2026-11-04/83a37233/commit.patch`), so this is a recurring property of the guard's measurement path, not a one-off.\n\nTHE CONFIGURED COMMAND is `guards.test_command: bash tests/selftest.sh` with `guards.tests: true` (`.gitreins/config.yaml`). No shipped check compares the guard's reported exit code with a direct run, and no board row covered this before this one (`grep -c 'Bad substitution' .coding-hermes/board/*.jsonl` = 0 at `8e1e312`).\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: every closure in this repo cites a verdict as its evidence. If a verdict's tier1 PASS can coexist with a non-zero measured exit, then \"tier1 PASS\" is not a claim about the test suite, and closures built on it inherit that ambiguity — the same class as CF-074 (closure evidence a stranger cannot resolve) and CF-076 (a PASS bound to a commit that cannot contain the graded change).","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce and attribute: run the guard's own test measurement at a fixed tip and record the exit code it reports for `bash tests/selftest.sh`; then run the same command directly at the same tip. The two numbers must appear in the evidence text. At `1d632d9` the direct run is `SELFTEST: PASS` exit 0 (three runs, logs named in the row's reasoning) while verdict `eb659af6` reports exit 2 plus a `/bin/sh: 1: Bad substitution` line, so today the pair disagrees.\n1. Attribution is mandatory, not prose: name the process that emits `/bin/sh: 1: Bad substitution` (the guard wrapper, a stub inside the suite, or a background child). If it is the guard, this row is refiled against gitreins and closed here as `moved`; if it is the suite, the suite must stop printing it.\n2. The gate refuses the ambiguity: a Tier-1 `tests` scanner whose measured exit code is non-zero must record outcome FAIL and name the exit code, with no prose exemption. A `verdict.json` with `tier1.tests.outcome == PASS` and a recorded non-zero test exit is a defect.\n3. A committed check ships in this tree (`scripts/` plus a `tests/selftest.sh` arm) that parses one or more `verdict.json` files and exits nonzero, printing a named `FAIL gate-exit-code` row, when a PASS outcome sits beside a non-zero recorded test exit.\n4. Red arm kept in the gate: a fixture verdict carrying `tier1 PASS` + `exit 2` makes the check exit nonzero and name the file; the same fixture with `exit 0` prints `PASS gate-exit-code` and exits 0. Both outputs are recorded in an evidence artifact in the tree.\n5. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` and exits 0 with no `Bad substitution` line anywhere in its output at the closing tip, and the new arm is counted in the section census.","probe":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T09:48:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T09:48:06Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"0570bc81abd965fdafa97a141f4ff7037510e707c13841d5f65aa83b9c15d2aa"}}
+{"id":"CF-192","title":"P3 \u2014 install-hermes.sh turns its own public-bind auth gate OFF when a listener already occupies the port: --apply prints PASS port / PASS status_probe / HERMES: PASS on a config with no basic_auth","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-04T09:57:29Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T09:57:29Z","detail":null,"reasoning":"`scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh:251` runs `check_public_bind_auth` and the gateway start only inside `if ! (command -v ss && ss -tln | grep -q \":$PORT \" )`. When anything already listens on the port, that whole branch is skipped: the adapter certifies `PASS  port \u2014 listening on :10800` and `PASS  status_probe \u2014 /api/status -> 200` from a listener it did not install and never auth-checked, then exits 0 with `HERMES: PASS`. CF-071's 19-arm fixture set stubs `ss` as `exit 1` (`tests/selftest.sh:386`), so every config arm exercises the free-port branch only: the gate's own subject is untested exactly where the gate is disabled. A node re-installed on a host whose port still holds a leftover unauthenticated gateway therefore reads green from the adapter.\n\nBoundary: distinct from CF-071 (grades the config PARSER; all 19 of its arms run on a free port), CF-150 (no step stages `basic_auth` at all), CF-092/CF-093 (README status rows are enforced by nothing). This row grades the CONDITION that disables CF-071's gate.","acceptance_criteria":"0. AC0 \u2014 reproduce at the filing tip from the repo root: the `probe` field prints the four lines under *today* (`PASS  port \u2014 listening on :10800`, `PASS  status_probe \u2014 /api/status -> 200`, `HERMES: PASS`, `auth_refusal_rows=0`) and exits 0. Re-derive the numbers at your own tip; do not copy the four lines as a fixed expectation of the fix.\n1. AC1 \u2014 a `tests/selftest.sh` arm drives the occupied-port branch: with a listener stub answering on `:PORT` and a config carrying NO `basic_auth`, `--apply` must NOT print `HERMES: PASS`. It must print either the existing auth refusal or a NAMED row stating the listener was not started by this adapter and its auth is unverified (e.g. `  FAIL  port \u2014 listening on :10800 (not started by this adapter; auth unverified)`), and exit nonzero. The arm's red proof is the pre-fix tree; the green proof is the fixed tree, both printed.\n2. AC2 \u2014 the same arm keeps the two existing green paths green in one run: free port + valid `basic_auth` still reaches `PASS gateway_start \u2014 /api/status -> 200`; free port + no `basic_auth` still prints the exact refusal wording CF-071 pinned.\n3. AC3 \u2014 `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` and `bash scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK` at the landing commit, and the fix is pushed with `git rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD` = 0.","probe":"d=$(mktemp -d); mkdir -p \"$d/bin\" \"$d/h/.hermes\" \"$d/h/hermes-venv/bin\"; printf '%s\\n' '#!/bin/sh' 'echo \"hermes 0.19.0\"' > \"$d/bin/hermes\"; printf '%s\\n' '#!/bin/sh' 'if [ \"$1\" = --version ]; then echo \"Python 3.12.3\"; exit 0; fi' 'exec python3 \"$@\"' > \"$d/bin/python\"; printf '%s\\n' '#!/bin/sh' 'echo \"LISTEN 0 4096 0.0.0.0:10800 0.0.0.0:*\"' > \"$d/bin/ss\"; printf '%s\\n' '#!/bin/sh' 'echo 200' > \"$d/bin/curl\"; chmod +x \"$d/bin/\"*; cp \"$d/bin/hermes\" \"$d/h/hermes-venv/bin/hermes\"; cp \"$d/bin/python\" \"$d/h/hermes-venv/bin/python\"; printf '%s\\n' 'dashboard:' '  port: 10800' > \"$d/h/.hermes/config.yaml\"; printf '%s\\n' 'DEMO_API_KEY=x' > \"$d/h/.hermes/.env\"; out=$(env PATH=\"$d/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$d/h\" HERMES_PYTHON_BIN=\"$d/bin/python\" HERMES_PIN=0.19.0 NODE_GATEWAY_PORT=10800 bash scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh --apply 2>&1); printf '%s\\n' \"$out\" | grep -E 'port \u2014|status_probe|HERMES:|needs dashboard'; echo \"auth_refusal_rows=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$out\" | grep -c 'needs dashboard.basic_auth')\"; rm -rf \"$d\""}
